                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8a87cc65-051f-3895-ac79-db61bde481f0",
                        "entry_id": "18ab4078-7c8d-384c-9fb7-57aeffff5a51",
                        "glosses": [
                            "биол. включающий в пределах одного вида резко отличных по облику особей, не имеющих переходных форм"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9f842755-f294-493b-8d00-f3b7c30a21cc",
                                "sense_id": "8a87cc65-051f-3895-ac79-db61bde481f0",
                                "text": "Характерной чертой описываемой флоры является обилие чрезвычайно полиморфных, богатых видами родов (акация — 486 видов, эвкалипт — 342, банксия — 50 и т. п.)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a06c4b9a-a090-3536-89d4-d669c74fb209",
                        "entry_id": "18ab4078-7c8d-384c-9fb7-57aeffff5a51",
                        "glosses": [
                            "хим. способный кристаллизоваться в различных формах"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b5b5e5b8-72dc-3bbf-8831-47d292e3e6a4",
                        "entry_id": "18ab4078-7c8d-384c-9fb7-57aeffff5a51",
                        "glosses": [
                            "комп. существующий в различных вариантах реализации (о программном объекте)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9cde9f6c-c0b7-42c6-a5da-cc237ad19dbf",
                        "source_entry_id": "18ab4078-7c8d-384c-9fb7-57aeffff5a51",
                        "target_lang_word": "polymorphic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "polymorphic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6af85670-dc96-3c54-8958-dcb77ea78418",
                                        "entry_id": "3efd13ad-8c34-3cec-b5d4-930aae7e13cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relating to polymorphism (any sense), able to have several shapes or forms."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b731374c-91be-4e6e-ac67-2e845af49725",
                                                "sense_id": "6af85670-dc96-3c54-8958-dcb77ea78418",
                                                "text": "I refer to those genera which have sometimes been called \"protean\" or \"polymorphic,\" in which the species present an inordinate amount of variation; and hardly two naturalists can agree which forms to rank as species and which as varieties."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be3a868f-5346-49e8-8787-d4dbe3bb46af",
                                                "sense_id": "6af85670-dc96-3c54-8958-dcb77ea78418",
                                                "text": "1897, Grant Allen, An African Millionaire\nDr. Beddersley came -- a dapper little man, with pent-house eyebrows, and keen, small eyes, whom I suspected at sight of being Colonel Clay himself in another of his clever polymorphic embodiments."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "391e234f-0d74-3a78-83af-800f9a52cdfc",
                                        "entry_id": "3efd13ad-8c34-3cec-b5d4-930aae7e13cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having or relating to the ability to take multiple data types for a single parameter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c1c14d1-737c-46e8-8db2-755d1a9204c4",
                                                "sense_id": "391e234f-0d74-3a78-83af-800f9a52cdfc",
                                                "text": "Polymorphic redefinition in C++ is achieved by the use of virtual functions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "828740a3-04cb-4d4f-bcfb-220eb6c1ca56",
                                                "sense_id": "391e234f-0d74-3a78-83af-800f9a52cdfc",
                                                "text": "A polymorphic call looks like a procedural call, but where a procedural call has only one possible target subroutine, a polymorphic call can result in the execution of one of several different subroutines."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4e337f07-7560-3f18-9035-fbb9096f99b1",
                                        "entry_id": "3efd13ad-8c34-3cec-b5d4-930aae7e13cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relating to a compound that can crystallizes into two or more distinct forms (e.g. carbon, which can crystalize into coal, graphite, diamond, etc.)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "042fc606-5a2f-4815-9a80-beb5e5b1d937",
                                                "sense_id": "4e337f07-7560-3f18-9035-fbb9096f99b1",
                                                "text": "The fact that polymorphic equilibrium is not a dynamic equilibrium is significant with respect to the random distribution of velocity of temperature agitation among the molecules."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e484de1e-0b05-48b3-ae97-51e9a63ba12c",
                        "source_entry_id": "18ab4078-7c8d-384c-9fb7-57aeffff5a51",
                        "target_lang_word": "polymorphous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "polymorphous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03a243c0-2ad3-3b36-b2f5-7863b034f667",
                                        "entry_id": "8cd49502-e29c-374e-b504-f8c377c73bf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having, or assuming, a variety of forms, characters, or styles"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd341256-4d98-4fb7-a739-c9dd20752b2f",
                                                "sense_id": "03a243c0-2ad3-3b36-b2f5-7863b034f667",
                                                "text": "Idealism is an exceedingly complex system, varying much with varying authors, very polymorphous, and consequently very difficult to discuss."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4c911a0a-107f-3fd9-9042-42b6e8f29a0b",
                                        "entry_id": "8cd49502-e29c-374e-b504-f8c377c73bf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having, or occurring in, several distinct forms"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e44c3511-a1e5-4748-b997-d452c2ae8b03",
                                                "sense_id": "4c911a0a-107f-3fd9-9042-42b6e8f29a0b",
                                                "text": "1913, R. Chodat in Popular Science Monthly Volume 82 Janauay 1913, A Grain of Wheat\nIn order to establish itself in any locality a plant must hold its own against competitors which, masters of the soil from time immemorial, have been selected to fit the soil and climate. Moreover, emmer is not cultivated anywhere in Palestine. This wild wheat is furthermore a different plant from any known in cultivation, a polymorphous race, no doubt, but a distinct one."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "83c7e21f-61e5-3db1-a3c6-adf7cba4dc20",
                                        "entry_id": "8cd49502-e29c-374e-b504-f8c377c73bf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Crystallizing in two or more different forms; polymorphic"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "10c14812-7f2c-4c10-b257-4eb9bfd5864e",
                        "source_entry_id": "18ab4078-7c8d-384c-9fb7-57aeffff5a51",
                        "target_lang_word": "polimorfo",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f21e0c69-bda9-41ae-9871-4040bc8d5ae7",
                        "source_entry_id": "18ab4078-7c8d-384c-9fb7-57aeffff5a51",
                        "target_lang_word": "polimorfo",
                        "target_lang_code": "it",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "polimorfo",
